 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Most people just toss it down a deep hole, as it's heavy to carry in, and you don't need it every night. Then little more than water used per person per day. A typical family of four might use two liters of water a day. A ten day trip would need to find ten liters of water per person. Try to recycle them as much as possible. Turn them into juice instead of straight water, or use them to wash out cups. Roughly one cup of water per person per day. Short trips can usually use water from cooking, so it' not that bad. You've already beat the biggest two, leaving the wash at home, and reusing food scraps. Well done.",
